            <ArticleTitle>Targeting &quot;hydrolytic&quot; activity of the S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine hydrolase.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>307-16</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Substrates that are specific for the &quot;hydrolytic&quot; activities of AdoHcy hydrolase have been recently identified. Upon interaction with the AdoHcy hydrolase such substrates generate the &quot;active&quot; electrophiles which then react with the enzyme nucleophiles to produce covalent inhibition. Dihalohomovinyl and haloacetylene analogues derived from adenosine as well 5'-S-allenyl-5'--thioadenosine derivative have been characterized as the first type II mechanism-based inhibitors of AdoHcy hydrolase that rely only on the &quot;hydrolytic&quot; activity. Design and synthesis of the novel adenine nucleosides as well their interaction with AdoHcy hydrolase are discussed in this review.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
